window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-cbf20fce235d2c96"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"get-from-idea-to-proof-of-concept\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">从想法到概念验证</h1> <p>先用 ImageGen 探索视觉方向，再构建想法的第一个版本。</p> <p>使用 Codex 与 ImageGen 把粗略想法转化为视觉方向，实现最小可用原型，并在浏览器中验证。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>与其只看书面计划，不如先快速实现原型来验证的早期产品构想。</li> <li>需要先进行视觉探索的 Web 应用、仪表板和工具。</li> <li>希望先用可运行的原型验证产品想法，再决定是否继续投入的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>在 Codex 开始实现前，使用 <code>gpt-image-2</code> 生成视觉概念、UI 样稿、素材方向和不同变体。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright（需联网）</a></td> <td>在真实浏览器中打开运行中的应用，检查变更路由，并逐项验证每次 UI 调整。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>为新网站、仪表板和前端原型采用先探索概念、再实现的工作流程，随后在浏览器中验证实现。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/game-studio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">game-studio（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果概念验证是浏览器游戏，可用 Game Studio 确定可玩的循环、素材流程、HUD、游戏引擎和试玩步骤。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建概念验证版本</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请先使用 ImageGen 为下面的想法生成高质量 UI 样稿，然后使用 [Build Web Apps plugin/Game studio plugin]（Build Web Apps 插件/游戏开发插件）来实现：\n\n[describe the idea, target user, and the main workflow]（描述这个想法、目标用户和主要工作流程）\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/image-generation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">图像生成指南（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-visual-direction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">先确定视觉方向</h2> <p>GPT Image 2 很适合生成高质量 UI 样稿。探索新想法时，不必从空白页面开始，可以先通过图像生成确定一个视觉方向。</p> <p>你可以采用两种方式：</p> <ul> <li>使用 ImageGen 技能反复调整视觉方向；选定方案后，让 Codex 根据它构建原型。此时请切换到 Codex，开启新对话，并附上最终要实现的图片，而不是直接在 ChatGPT 对话中继续。让 Codex 参考你提供的图片附件，通常更有帮助。</li> <li>使用插件，只需描述你的想法；插件会为你生成视觉方向并处理后续步骤。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"leverage-a-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用插件</h2> <p>如果你不需要先反复调整视觉方向再开始实现，可以直接使用插件并描述想法。</p> <p>对于 Web 应用、仪表板、创意网站和以前端为主的工具，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps plugin（需联网）</a>。它会引导 Codex 先生成设计、在代码中还原设计，再通过浏览器将实现效果与构想进行对照。</p> <p>如果要构建浏览器游戏，请使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/game-studio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Game Studio plugin（需联网）</a>。在扩展游戏前，先明确玩家可以执行的动作、首个可玩循环、引擎、素材工作流、HUD、控制方式和浏览器测试。</p> <p><a id=\"iteration-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">迭代工作流</h2> <p>好的概念验证应限定在一个可快速实现、并能与团队一起验证的 MVP（最小可行产品）范围内。 如果想确认 MVP 是否符合预期，可以使用 Playwright interactive 让 Codex 验证工作成果。</p> <p>第一个版本可运行后，可以在同一对话中提出范围明确的修改要求：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a new [feature/bug fix/etc.]. Use Playwright interactive to verify your changes.\n\nFeedback to apply:\n[paste comments, screenshots, or review notes]\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">添加一项新的 [feature/bug fix/etc.]。使用 Playwright interactive 验证你的更改。\n\n需要采纳的反馈：\n[paste comments, screenshots, or review notes]</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"get-from-idea-to-proof-of-concept\">Get from idea to proof of concept</h1> <p>Explore the concept visually with ImageGen and build a first version of your idea.</p> <p>Use Codex with ImageGen to turn a rough idea into a visual direction, implement the smallest useful prototype, and verify it in a browser.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Early product ideas where a working prototype will answer more than a written plan.</li> <li>Web apps, dashboards, and tools that need visual exploration before implementation.</li> <li>Teams that want to validate a product idea with a working prototype before investing further.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$imagegen</code></td> <td>Generate visual concepts, UI mockups, asset directions, and variants with <code>gpt-image-2</code> before Codex implements the selected direction.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/playwright-interactive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$playwright (online)</a></td> <td>Open the running app in a real browser, inspect the changed route, and verify each small UI adjustment before the next iteration.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-web-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the concept-first workflow for new web apps, dashboards, sites, and frontend prototypes, then verify the implementation in the browser.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/game-studio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">game-studio (online)</a></td> <td>Use Game Studio when the proof of concept is a browser game and needs a playable loop, asset workflow, HUD, engine choice, and playtest pass.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build the Proof of Concept</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use ImageGen to generate a high quality UI mockup for the following idea, then use the [Build Web Apps plugin/Game studio plugin] to implement it:\n\n[describe the idea, target user, and the main workflow]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/image-generation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Image generation guide (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-with-a-visual-direction\">Start with a visual direction</h2> <p>GPT Image 2 is great at generating high quality UI mockups. Instead of starting from scratch when exploring new ideas, you can leverage image generation to get a visual direction.</p> <p>You can do this in two ways:</p> <ul> <li>Iterate on the visual direction using the ImageGen skill, and once you are satisfied with the proposed UI, you can ask Codex to build a prototype matching the visuals. In that case, select Codex, start a new chat, and attach the final image you want to implement rather than continuing the ChatGPT chat directly. Codex does better when it can reference a user attachment.</li> <li>Use a plugin and simply describe your idea: the plugin will generate the visual direction for you and handle next steps.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"leverage-a-plugin\">Leverage a plugin</h2> <p>If you do not need to iterate on the visual direction before starting the implementation, you can use a plugin and describe your idea.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-web-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build Web Apps plugin (online)</a> for web apps, dashboards, creative websites, and frontend-heavy tools. Its workflow pushes Codex to generate a design first, match it in code, and use the browser to compare the result back to the concept.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/game-studio\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Game Studio plugin (online)</a> when the proof of concept is a browser game. That path should define the player verbs, first playable loop, engine, asset workflow, HUD, controls, and browser test before expanding the game.</p> <h2 id=\"iteration-workflow\">Iteration workflow</h2> <p>A good proof of concept is scoped to an MVP that can be implemented quickly and validated with the team. If you want to make sure the MVP is working as expected, you can use Playwright interactive to let Codex verify its work.</p> <p>Once you have a first version working, you can iterate on it by asking for scoped changes in the same chat:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a new [feature/bug fix/etc.]. Use Playwright interactive to verify your changes.\n\nFeedback to apply:\n[paste comments, screenshots, or review notes]\n</code></pre>"};
